From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: MAINTAINERS: cover page-cache and writeback helper headers
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:30:41 -0800

Cover buffer-head and multi-page page-cache I/O, folio queues and writeback
completion-proportion accounting under PAGE CACHE.  Share the I/O iterator
implementation, API headers and tests with USER ACCESS: they also handle
page-cache, XArray and folio-queue buffers.

Add the following file assignments:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - PAGE CACHE
        include/linux/buffer_head.h
        include/linux/flex_proportions.h
        include/linux/folio_queue.h
        include/linux/iov_iter.h
        include/linux/mpage.h
        include/linux/uio.h
        lib/flex_proportions.c
        lib/iov_iter.c
        lib/tests/kunit_iov_iter.c

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Matthew Wilcox (Oracle) <willy@infradead.org>
Cc: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Cc: Al Viro <viro@zeniv.linux.org.uk>
---

